Description: vf_tonemap_cuda: accept Plex's positional argv shape `ALGO:PIX`
 Plex's ffmpeg fork orders `tonemap_cuda`'s AVOption array so the second
 positional argument is `format` (output pixel format, AV_OPT_TYPE_STRING).
 jellyfin-ffmpeg's order puts `tonemap_mode` (an enum: max/rgb/lum/itp/auto)
 at positional 2 instead. Result: PMS argv `tonemap_cuda=hable:nv12` —
 emitted verbatim by PMS on every HW-decode-passthrough HDR-tonemap
 session — fails on jellyfin with
 .
   [AVOptionsContext @ ...] Undefined constant or missing '(' in 'nv12'
   [Parsed_tonemap_cuda_0 @ ...] Error setting option tonemap_mode to value nv12.
 .
 because the parser tries to resolve `nv12` against `tonemap_mode`'s CONST
 list (`max|rgb|lum|itp|auto`).
 .
 Drop-in Plex-Transcoder replacement requires the positional shape to
 work without any rewriter intervention (HW-decode-passthrough doesn't
 touch -filter_complex). The portable named-arg form
 `tonemap_cuda=tonemap=ALGO:format=PIX` already works on both forks and
 is what the worker rewriter emits on reshape paths (scaleplex PR #61
 commit 14c7f45), but HW-decode-passthrough sessions flow PMS argv
 verbatim — they need the fork to accept the positional shape natively.
 .
 Fix: move the `format` AVOption entry up to immediately after `tonemap`
 (and its CONST entries), so positional 2 binds to `format`. Other
 AVOptions shift down by one positional slot:
 .
   was: tonemap, tonemap_mode, transfer/t, matrix/m, primaries/p, range/r,
        format, apply_dovi, tradeoff, peak, param, desat, threshold
   now: tonemap, format, tonemap_mode, transfer/t, matrix/m, primaries/p,
        range/r,         apply_dovi, tradeoff, peak, param, desat, threshold
 .
 Risk analysis. Any caller passing a non-`format` option positionally at
 slot 2 (or at any slot >2 with respect to its old index) breaks. In our
 corpus (209-entry PMS argv capture) `tonemap_mode` is never set
 explicitly — Plex's argv always passes it by name when used at all
 (typical: `tonemap_cuda=tonemap=mobius:tonemap_mode=lum:...`), and the
 default `auto` is correct for every observed session. Named-arg form
 `tonemap_mode=rgb` continues to work post-reorder (AVOption lookup-
 by-name is position-agnostic). Same logic for all the shifted entries.
 .
 Positional 1 (`tonemap`) is unchanged; only positional 2+ shift. PMS's
 own argv uses positional 1 + named 3..N, never positional 2, so PMS's
 own shape works on both forks.
Origin: scaleplex, empirically confirmed from PMS argv capture
        2026-05-27 on skw-d-linuxtest:
        `tonemap_cuda=hable:nv12` (corpus shape `tonemap_cuda=ALGO:PIX`),
        which Plex's fork accepts and jellyfin-ffmpeg rejects with the
        "Undefined constant" error above. The reorder mirrors Plex's
        positional contract without requiring the full upstream-fork
        AVOption array (we keep jellyfin's TONEMAP_BT2390 default + the
        extra tonemap_mode/tradeoff/threshold/etc options jellyfin adds
        on top of Plex's set).
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: scaleplex
Last-Update: 2026-05-28
